# Ship changes without asking

When the user asks for a site change, implement it, then commit, `git push origin main`, and rely on Vercel auto-deploy. Do not ask whether to commit, push, or deploy.

Do not ask the user to approve routine git or terminal commands in chat. Request the permissions the tools need and continue. Only stop and ask if the action is harmful: secrets in git, force-push, deleting the repo, rewriting published history, or destroying production data.

Commit messages stay short and explain why. Never skip hooks. Never change git config.
